.TH UFW 1 "December 2024" "Network Security" "Lab Commands"
.SH NAME
ufw \- Customized UFW commands for Network Security Lab
.SH DESCRIPTION
This manual provides simplified UFW commands needed in common
network security lab scenarios (Lab Sheet 8: Part 0 & Part 2).
.SH COMMANDS
.SS Enable / Status / Reset
.TP
.B sudo ufw enable
Enable the firewall.
.TP
.B sudo ufw status numbered
Show active rules with numbers.
.TP
.B sudo ufw disable
Disable the firewall.
.SS Basic Rules
.TP
.B Allow SSH
sudo ufw allow ssh
.br
(or sudo ufw allow 22/tcp)
.TP
.B Block a port
sudo ufw deny 80/tcp
.TP
.B Allow a port with protocol
sudo ufw allow 8080/tcp
.TP
.B Delete a rule
sudo ufw delete NUM
.SH LAB CHALLENGES
.SS 1. Block all incoming traffic (default deny)
.TP
sudo ufw default deny incoming
.br
sudo ufw allow icmp from any
.br
(Allow only ping)
.SS 2. Allow only port 8080/tcp
.TP
sudo ufw default deny incoming
.br
sudo ufw allow 8080/tcp
.SS 3. Deny SSH from a specific subnet
.TP
sudo ufw deny from 192.168.1.0/24 to any port 22 proto tcp
.SH AUTHOR
Exam preparation cheat-sheet.

